---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Src from '../components/Src.astro';
import Aff from '../components/Aff.astro';
import Unverified from '../components/Unverified.astro';
import { S } from '../data/sources.js';
const title = 'iPostal1 Pricing Explained: What $9.99 Gets You, Every Tier, and Every Extra Fee';
const description = 'iPostal1 plans run from $9.99 to $69.99 a month before location surcharges. All 12 plan tiers, the Select/Premium/Prestige address add-ons, the $2.25 scan fee, storage fees and the $25 Form 1583 notary, copied from iPostal1\'s own pricing pages.';
const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":title,"description":description,"dateModified":"2026-11-20"};
---
<Base title={title} description={description} updated="2026-11-20" schema={schema}>
  <h1>iPostal1 pricing, explained</h1>
  <p class="lede">The $9.99 iPostal1 plan is real, but it gets you 30 envelope images a month at a Standard address, for personal mail only. Opening a letter costs $2.25, and a business name means the $14.99 plan. Below is every published tier and fee, copied from iPostal1's pricing pages on November 20, 2026.</p>

  <h2>The three plan families</h2>
  <p>iPostal1 sells three kinds of plans. Each has four tiers that differ only by how many mail items you get a month <Src href={S.ipVma} label="VMA" /> <Src href={S.ipVba} label="VBA" /> <Src href={S.ipVo} label="VO" />.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Mail items / month</th><th>Virtual Mailing Address (personal)</th><th>Virtual Business Address</th><th>Virtual Office (phone + fax)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>30</td><td>$9.99/mo or $99/yr <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td><td>$14.99/mo or $149/yr <Src href={S.ipVba} /></td><td>n/a</td></tr>
      <tr><td>60</td><td>$14.99/mo or $149/yr <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td><td>$19.99/mo or $199/yr <Src href={S.ipVba} /></td><td>$39.99/mo or $399/yr, local number <Src href={S.ipVo} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>120</td><td>$24.99/mo or $249/yr <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td><td>$29.99/mo or $299/yr <Src href={S.ipVba} /></td><td>$49.99/mo local, or $59.99/mo toll-free <Src href={S.ipVo} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>240</td><td>$39.99/mo or $399/yr <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td><td>$44.99/mo or $449/yr <Src href={S.ipVba} /></td><td>$69.99/mo or $699/yr, toll-free <Src href={S.ipVo} /></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>The yearly price works out to ten months of the monthly price. iPostal1 calls it "2 Months Free" <Src href={S.ipVma} />. All three families have no contract, and you can change plans every month <Src href={S.ipVma} />.</p>

  <h2>Personal vs business: the $5 difference that matters</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Virtual Mailing Address</strong> plans are "for personal use only." They include up to 6 recipient names but "no company name" <Src href={S.ipFaq} label="FAQ" /> <Src href={S.ipVma} />.</li>
    <li><strong>Virtual Business Address</strong> plans add 1 company name (still up to 6 recipients) <Src href={S.ipVba} />. iPostal1 says to use these to "register your business" <Src href={S.ip} />.</li>
    <li><strong>Virtual Office</strong> plans add a local or toll-free phone number and a fax number. Calls are metered: inbound calls to a local number cost $0.015 a minute, forwarding to a U.S. number costs $0.02 a minute, and voicemail beyond 250 free minutes costs $0.01 a minute <Src href={S.ipVo} />.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If mail will arrive in an LLC's name, the real entry price is $14.99, not $9.99. See <a href="/virtual-mailbox-for-llc/">using a virtual mailbox for an LLC</a>.</p>

  <h2>Why your address may cost more than $9.99</h2>
  <p>iPostal1 says roughly 90% of its locations are "Standard" addresses that start at $9.99 a month. Addresses "in prestigious buildings or in locations where costs and demand are higher" cost more <Src href={S.ipFaq} label="FAQ" />:</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Address type</th><th>Surcharge (as published)</th><th>30-item personal plan would be</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Standard</td><td>none</td><td>$9.99</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Select</td><td>+$10</td><td>$19.99 <Unverified note="assumes surcharge is per month" /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Premium</td><td>+$20</td><td>$29.99 <Unverified note="assumes surcharge is per month" /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Prestige</td><td>+$30</td><td>$39.99 <Unverified note="assumes surcharge is per month" /></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>The FAQ doesn't say whether the surcharge is per month or whether it changes on yearly billing <Src href={S.ipFaq} label="FAQ" />. Check the price shown for your chosen address at checkout.</p>

  <h2>Pay-per-use fees (all plan families)</h2>
  <p>These are the same on all three U.S. pricing pages. iPostal1 notes they don't apply to Canadian locations <Src href={S.ipVma} />.</p>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Envelope image of every item</td><td>Included <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mail items over your plan's limit</td><td>$0.35 per item <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Open and scan, or shred (1 envelope = 1 order)</td><td>$2.25 for up to 10 pages, then $0.25 per page <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Prepaid scan/shred bundles (no expiry, non-refundable)</td><td>$10 for 5 · $18 for 10 · $30 for 20 <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Discard (recycle) an item</td><td>Included <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Forwarding</td><td>Real-time shipping price for the carrier you pick. Consolidating letters is free; $1.95 per package or letter-pack consolidated <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Check deposit by mail (most locations)</td><td>$4.95 for up to 5 checks, plus check scans and trackable shipping <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Photos of a package's invoice / contents</td><td>$2.95 / $3.95 / both $5.95 <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Extra shipping insurance</td><td>$4 per $100 <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Receive a fax</td><td>$2 for up to 6 pages, then $0.25/page <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pickup at the mail center</td><td>"Some locations charge a nominal fee" <Src href={S.ipVma} /> <Unverified note="amount set per location" /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Send mail (letters / postcards)</td><td>From $0.85 / from $1.19 <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Registered agent add-on (business plans; 25 states + DC listed)</td><td>$99 per year <Src href={S.ip} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>AI and live call answering add-on</td><td>From $49 a month <Src href={S.ipVma} /></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Free storage, then storage fees</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Letters, letter-packs and packages under 12×12×12 in.: 30 days free. Packages up to 24×17×12 in.: 10 days. Bigger packages: 5 days <Src href={S.ipVma} />.</li>
    <li>After that, letters, large envelopes, magazines and postcards cost $1.10 per item per month. Packages cost $1.10 per pound (actual or dimensional weight, whichever is greater) per month, per 10 days or per 5 days, depending on size <Src href={S.ipVma} />.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>One-time costs</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Form 1583:</strong> the online notary costs $25. You can also sign in person at many mail centers, and some charge "a small fee" for that. Customers living outside the U.S. must use the online notary <Src href={S.ipFaq} label="FAQ" />. Why some other providers skip the notary entirely: <a href="/usps-form-1583-online-notarization/">Form 1583 rules</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Refunds:</strong> a full refund within the first 30 days "upon request, if account not used." Plans renew unless you cancel before the billing date <Src href={S.ipVma} />.</li>
    <li>Prices are "plus applicable taxes" <Src href={S.ipVma} />.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What a typical month costs</h2>
  <p>Say you get 25 items a month at a Standard address, open 4 letters (under 10 pages each) and recycle the rest:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Personal 30-item plan: $9.99 + 4 × $2.25 = <strong>$18.99</strong> <Src href={S.ipVma} />.</li>
    <li>Same usage with the 10-pack bundle ($1.80 per order): $9.99 + 4 × $1.80 = <strong>$17.19</strong>, once you've paid $18 up front <Src href={S.ipVma} />.</li>
    <li>Business 30-item plan: $14.99 + $9.00 = <strong>$23.99</strong> <Src href={S.ipVba} />.</li>
    <li>First month: add $25 for the online notary, unless you sign in person <Src href={S.ipFaq} label="FAQ" />.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you open most of your mail, a plan with scans included can cost less. Traveling Mailbox Basic is $15 with 35 page scans <Src href={S.tmb} />. See <a href="/cheapest-virtual-mailbox/">the cheapest virtual mailbox</a> and <a href="/ipostal1-vs-anytime-mailbox/">iPostal1 vs Anytime Mailbox</a>.</p>

  <ul>
    <li><Aff id="ipostal1" href="https://ipostal1.com/" text="iPostal1 plans and locations" /></li>
  </ul>
  <p>More: <a href="/virtual-mailbox-pricing-comparison/">all providers compared</a> · <a href="/">Mailbox Atlas home</a></p>
</Base>
